Subject: Modify R output in latex
Message-ID: <kmywC7VFTlY.EXOS7w61ebIJ@knitr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/knitr/c/kmywC7VFTlY/m/EXOS7w61ebIJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Using the default "latex" render, is there a way I can wrap the R
output in an "Soutput" environment?

I tried this:

knit_hooks$set(output=function(x, options) str_c("\\begin{Soutput}\n",
x, "\\end{Soutput}\n"))

But it doesn't seem to do anything.

